# Plan Build → commit subject

When finishing a **Plan → Build**, **implement the plan**, **execute the plan**, or equivalent — and when pausing for human review after one or more plan todos — end the handoff with a **commit subject line** for the changelog since the last such pause (or since the build started).

## When

| Situation | What to include |
|-----------|-----------------|
| Entire plan build finished | One subject covering all work in that build |
| Per-todo / staged execution, pause for review | One subject covering **only** the changes in this pause |

## Format

Follow [commit-subject-category.mdc](commit-subject-category.mdc) — one pasteable line:

```text
docs: …
```

## Rules

- Always provide the subject in the handoff; do **not** create the commit unless the user explicitly asks ([no-unrequested-commits.mdc](no-unrequested-commits.mdc)).
- Subject summarizes **why** / outcome for the current changelog, not a file list.
- If there are no file changes in the pause, say so and omit a subject (or say `n/a`).
- If CI gates ran for that pause, keep the usual gate note; still include the subject when there are changes.
